{"shortDescription":"Spot basis bids for soybeans and corn were steady to mixed in the US Midwest on Wednesday, with some processors sharply improving their basis for immediate delivery of soybeans amid tightening supplies in some regions, spot checks showed.Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures in cts/bu:NOTE…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Spot basis bids for soybeans and corn were steady to mixed in the US Midwest on Wednesday, with some processors sharply improving their basis for immediate delivery of soybeans amid tightening supplies in some regions, spot checks showed."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The spot basis for soybeans at a crushing facility in Morristown, Indiana, jumped from zero to 25 cents a bushel over Chicago Board of Trade November (SX26) soybean futures, reflecting strong demand for soybeans delivered into the region's processing plants this week."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Excessive rains in the area, as well as across central Indiana, have caused significant harvest delays and created muddy fields that have prevented farmers from harvesting their crops in the area."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Local corn and soybean farmers are reporting that heavy rains in August have left their crops heavily saturated, and have slowed down the natural dry-down process — which in turn is pushing back their crops' maturity dates by several weeks."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, recent storms dumped up to seven inches of rain over northeastern Indiana, particularly around the Upper Wabash River Basin, and created flash flood conditions, snarled transportation routes and left low-lying crop fields submerged."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["In contrast, the soybean basis weakened 10 cents a bushel at a river terminal in Toledo, Ohio."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{